  "analysis": "We need to solve the Matryoshka problem. Each doll i has dimensions (xi, yi, zi). We may rotate, so after sorting dimensions ascendingly (ai1 <= ai2 <= ai3) for inner doll i and (bj1 <= bj2 <= bj3) for outer doll j, i can be placed inside j if ai1 < bj1, ai2 < bj2, and ai3 < bj3. A doll can contain at most one other doll directly, but a doll can itself be inside another, forming chains. The sum to minimize is the total volume of dolls visible from outside, i.e., the sum of volumes of outermost dolls in each chain. This is equivalent to maximizing the total volume of dolls that are placed inside another doll, since total volume is fixed. We can model this as a maximum weight bipartite matching: left nodes are inner candidates i, right nodes are outer candidates j, edge (i, j) exists if i can fit in j with weight vol[i] = xi*yi*zi. A doll can be inside at most one other and can contain at most one direct doll, which matches a bipartite matching constraint. The answer is total_volume - max_inside_volume. We can solve this with a min-cost max-flow formulation: source -> each left node (capacity 1, cost 0); left i -> right j edge (capacity 1, cost = -vol[i]) if i fits in j; right nodes -> sink (capacity 1, cost 0). Running min-cost max-flow pushes as many negative-cost flows as beneficial, giving max total inside volume. The final answer for each dataset is total_volume - (-min_cost). Implementing in C++17 with SPFA-based min-cost max-flow handles N up to ~100 comfortably. The program will read multiple datasets until a line with 0. Output one line per dataset with the minimal visible sum.",
  "plan": "Steps to implement and run:\n1) Write a C++17 program matryoshka.cpp implementing the min-cost max-flow solution described above.\n2) Compile: g++ -std=c++17 matryoshka.cpp -O2 -o matryoshka\n3) Run with the sample input to verify correctness. Provide input ending with 0 on a separate line.\n4) If needed, test on additional cases by providing more datasets.\n5) The program prints one line per dataset with the minimal sum of visible doll volumes.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > matryoshka.cpp <<'CPP'\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nstruct Edge {\n    int to, rev, cap;\n    long long cost;\n};\n\nstruct MCMF {\n    int N;\n    vector<vector<Edge>> G;\n    MCMF(int n=0): N(n), G(n) {}\n    void init(int n){ N=n; G.assign(n, {}); }\n    void addEdge(int u, int v, int cap, long long cost){\n        Edge a{v, (int)G[v].size(), cap, cost};\n        Edge b{u, (int)G[u].size(), 0, -cost};\n        G[u].push_back(a);\n        G[v].push_back(b);\n    }\n    pair<int,long long> minCostMaxFlow(int s, int t){\n        int flow = 0; long long cost = 0;\n        const long long INF = (1LL<<60);\n        int n = N;\n        vector<long long> dist(n);\n        vector<int> pv(n), pe(n);\n        while(true){\n            fill(dist.begin(), dist.end(), INF);\n            vector<char> inq(n, 0);\n            deque<int> q;\n            dist[s] = 0; q.push_back(s); inq[s] = 1;\n            while(!q.empty()){\n                int u = q.front(); q.pop_front(); inq[u] = 0;\n                for(int i=0;i<(int)G[u].size();++i){\n                    Edge &e = G[u][i];\n                    if(e.cap>0 && dist[e.to] > dist[u] + e.cost){\n                        dist[e.to] = dist[u] + e.cost;\n                        pv[e.to] = u; pe[e.to] = i;\n                        if(!inq[e.to]){ inq[e.to]=1; q.push_back(e.to); }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            if(dist[t] == INF) break; // no more augmenting paths\n            int add = 1; int v = t;\n            while(v != s){ int u = pv[v], idx = pe[v]; add = min(add, G[u][idx].cap); v = u; }\n            v = t;\n            while(v != s){ int u = pv[v], idx = pe[v]; Edge &e = G[u][idx]; e.cap -= add; G[v][e.rev].cap += add; v = u; }\n            flow += add;\n            cost += dist[t] * add;\n        }\n        return {flow, cost};\n    }\n};\n\nint main(){\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    int N;\n    while ( (cin >> N) ) {\n        if (N == 0) break;\n        vector<array<int,3>> d(N);\n        vector<long long> vol(N);\n        long long total = 0;\n        for(int i=0;i<N;i++){\n            long long x,y,z; cin >> x >> y >> z;\n            array<int,3> arr = {(int)x,(int)y,(int)z};\n            sort(arr.begin(), arr.end());\n            d[i] = arr;\n            vol[i] = x * y * z;\n            total += vol[i];\n        }\n        int S = 0;\n        int Lstart = 1;\n        int Rstart = 1 + N;\n        int T = 1 + N + N;\n        int V = T + 1;\n        MCMF mf(V);\n        for(int i=0;i<N;i++) mf.addEdge(S, Lstart + i, 1, 0);\n        for(int j=0;j<N;j++) mf.addEdge(Rstart + j, T, 1, 0);\n        for(int i=0;i<N;i++){\n            for(int j=0;j<N;j++){\n                if(d[i][0] < d[j][0] && d[i][1] < d[j][1] && d[i][2] < d[j][2]){\n                    mf.addEdge(Lstart + i, Rstart + j, 1, -vol[i]);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        auto res = mf.minCostMaxFlow(S, T);\n        long long maxInside = -res.second;\n        long long ans = total - maxInside;\n        cout << ans << \"\\n\";\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\nCPP\n\n\ng++ -std=c++17 matryoshka.cpp -O2 -o matryoshka\n\n./matryoshka << 'EOF'\n2\n1 2 3\n4 2 3\n3\n2 5 2\n3 3 4\n5 5 5\n0\nEOF",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
